WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.748
This is the first thing the narrator

00:00:02.748 --> 00:00:03.999
says out loud.

00:00:04.199 --> 00:00:06.984
This is the second thing, and it

00:00:06.984 --> 00:00:09.589
runs a little longer than the first

00:00:09.589 --> 00:00:10.599
one did.

00:00:10.799 --> 00:00:12.944
To produce a single token the model

00:00:12.944 --> 00:00:16.399
reads seventy billion parameters out of memory.

00:00:16.599 --> 00:00:19.647
The arithmetic is trivial next to the

00:00:19.647 --> 00:00:21.740
move, so the chip spends its life

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:22.599
waiting.

00:00:22.798 --> 00:00:25.151
In practice this delivers two to three

00:00:25.151 --> 00:00:27.997
times the throughput on ordinary prose.

00:00:28.198 --> 00:00:31.154
Which is the lesson underneath all of

00:00:31.154 --> 00:00:33.681
it, and the reason the trick works

00:00:33.681 --> 00:00:34.598
at all.
